{"text": "Jefferson R. Thomas\n\nWork Experience\nState Strategist - Missouri, Kansas and Colorado, Majority Strategies,\nNovember 2016-Present\nOffice of General Counsel, Presidential Transition Team, Washington DC\nNovember 2016-February 2017\ne Assist Office of General Counsel with various projects\ne Assist in the development and execution of vetting and job placement procedures\ne Deploy to Wisconsin to manage recount effort\nColorado Political Director, Donald J. Trump for President, Denver, co\nJuly 2016-Conclusion of Campaign\ne Manage EDO for Colorado, overseeing legal teams and plans in Targeted Counties\ne Assist in the development and execution of state plan and budget\ne Worked with Campaign HQ on special projects as assigned by Senior Staff\nPolitical Director, Colorado Republican Committee, Denver, co\nMarch 2016-July 2016\ne Provided political assistance to state legislative candidates and daily guidance to targeted races\ne Assisted Chairman with budgeting and spending of state account for legislative races\ne Assisted Executive Director in planning, preparing, and executing Colorado State Convention in\nColorado Springs\nDeputy State Director, Colorado Victory Program, Colorado Republican Committee, Denver, CO\nJuly 2015- March 2016\ne Managed Regional Field Staff Daily, monitoring production of metrics and relationships\ne Assisted State Director with various project focusing on current political climate of Colorado for large\npresentations.\ne Supported 2015 Boulder Debate, providing volunteer infrastructure and management of over 100\nAdministrative Graduate Assistant, University of Missouri Football, Columbia, MO\nJune 2014-July 2015\ne Managed completion of daily administrative tasks for Head Football Coach and Director of Operations\ne Served as liaison to multiple departments involved in student athlete support such as Residential Life,\nAcademic Support, and Sports Medicine\n\u00a9 Coordinated all trip operations and logistics for 10-day Citrus Bowl trip to Orlando, FL for 175 players,\ncoaches, and support staff\nCampaign Manager, Bill Reineke for State Representative, Tiffin, OH\nMarch 2014- May 2014\n\u00a9 Most contested house primary in Ohio; 10 point victory in all write-in primary, 600 vote spread\ne Oversaw the successful implementation of $135,000.00 budget\ne Created operations strategy for general election campaign, including voter ID file and donor file\nPolitical Director, Barry Smitherman for Attorney General, Austin, Texas\nJanuary 2014-March 2014\n\u00a9 Managed field staff across the state to ensure event presence and prompt follow-up with grassroots\ne Implemented phone program that generated 100,000 phone calls using small calling force\nStrategically managed data collection and assessment for both phone program and early voting\nDavid Ramadan for Delegate, Loudoun County, Virginia\nOctober 2011 \u2014 November 2011\n\u00a9 Coordinated all field operations and EDO operations for the campaign\n\u00a9 Most competitive race in Virginia, winning by 51 votes\ne First delegate elected of Muslim background and first non-American-born delegate\nField Director, Better Leadership for Missouri PAC, Jefferson City, Missouri\nMay 2008 \u2014 May 2011\ne Assisted candidates with planning and executing grassroots strategies\n\u00a9 Traveled with Lieutenant Governor Kinder to area events, assisted with data analysis, and provided\nadvice necessary to build a network for his potential gubernatorial campaign in 2012",
